oing to make in this location  franchising is typically the faster way  to grow you want to take this big you  want to take this nationwide franchising  lets you get there because people are  paying you for the rights to open up  locations you want complete control of  business but you have all these kind of  independent people who are around the  country running this it's fast because  they're paying into it if you go own or  operate and you get investors involved  you have more say because you actually  own each store but you have the  challenge of bringing on partners who  you not have to work with instead of you  owning everything and you have the  challenge of slower growth because you  have to open one store at a time now  both methods can work if you look at two  of the biggest systems in the world  you've got starbucks and mcdonald's  we're starbucks everything is run by the  store you can't buy starbucks franchise  and mcdonald's is the opposite they're  all franchise if they have their  training university you learn about  making hamburgers and running a  restaurant but it's all franchisees so  it comes down to one what kind of  business do you want to run because i've  had a lot of successful entrepreneur  friends of mine who have gone the  franchising route and your business now  becomes working with franchisees and  training them instead of working with  the customer so most of your time is  spent talking to your franchisees and  recruiting them and training them and a  lot of the entrence have gone down that  road they don't like it they want to be  customer facing so there's not the kind  of business that you want to run or not  okay second how fast you want to grow  because if you want to get this going  quicker franchise and we'll get you  there faster because you don't need as  much of your own capital from investors  and from yourself people will supply the  capital you have to show you have a  working model people will supply the  capital the third one is do you want to  work with investors or not do you want  to have partners on board you know you  don't know I don't know how much you're  asking for I don't know much they're  going to take as a percentage of your  business but you know can you work with  a business partner do you want that or  not so both models can work hopefully  help give you a little bit of clarity it  comes down to  kind of business do you want to run and  how it you want to grow that will help  decide which model to take good luck and  believe and keep me posted with your  progress for those you watching like the  video please give it a thumbs up below  leave a comment I'll make a video  response subscribe to the channel if you  like what you've seen and I'll see you  soon
 

